     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily dose:** The maximum for prescription use is 3,200 mg/day. This order would give 6,400 mg/day. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Here are some common regimens:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum, usually for short-term use)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
