       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave is timing, not a clinical need for this dose. At 6,400 mg/day, the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming the dose doesn't change that risk.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 600 mg PO every 6 hours. Tell me which you want and I'll enter it.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy or the team:** I can attach a note to a standard-dose order if you want something flagged before evening rounds.\n- **Get a quick review:** A pharmacist or attending can approve a higher dose if there is a documented reason I don't know about. I can't think of a recognized indication for 1,600 mg per dose.\n\nIf the goal is to settle pain control before evening rounds, I can also help with a multimodal plan, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen. You would need to choose and confirm that plan."
      }
